Origin

mojo-align is an open-source GPU/CPU reimplementation of published bisulfite
alignment methods, not a closed proprietary product.

- Linear WGBS (`fq2bam-meth`) follows the published bwa-meth approach
  (https://github.com/brentp/bwa-meth; MIT).
- Pangenome WGBS orchestration (`methylgrapher/`) is derived from methylGrapher
  (MIT; Ting Wang Lab). See methylgrapher/LICENSE and methylgrapher/NOTICE.
- Graph mapping (`giraffe/`) follows published vg giraffe / GBZ methods (MIT
  upstream tooling at runtime).

Runtime dependencies (Mojo/MAX toolchain, vg, samtools, bwa) remain under
their own licenses and are not re-licensed here.
